.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt USERMGMT.CONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm usermgmt.conf
.Nd defaults for new accounts
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The file
.Pa /etc/usermgmt.conf
holds the defaults
.Xr useradd 8 ,
.Xr groupadd 8
and
.Xr pw 8
use for what a command line leaves out.
It is the
.Nx
and
.Ox
file;
.Xr pw 8
reads it in place of
.Fx Ns 's
.Pa pw.conf .
If it is missing, every default below holds.
.Pp
Each line is a key and a value separated by white space;
.Ql #
starts a comment.
An unknown key or bad value is warned about and ignored.
.Bl -tag -width "skel_dir"
.It Cm base_dir
The directory new homes are made in.
Default
.Pa /home .
.It Cm class
The
.Xr login.conf 5
class.
Default empty, meaning
.Ql default .
.It Cm expire
When new accounts expire, in any form
.Xr useradd 8 Ns 's
.Fl e
takes.
Default empty: never.
.It Cm group
The primary group: a name, a group ID, or
.Ql =uid
for a new group named like the user.
Default
.Ql =uid .
.It Cm homeperm
The mode of new home directories, in octal.
Default 0755.
.It Cm inactive
Accepted and kept, but unused: OxideBSD records no inactive time.
.It Cm password
The
.Xr crypt 3
hash new accounts get.
Default
.Ql * ,
no usable password.
.It Cm preserve
Accepted for
.Nx
files; ignored.
.It Cm range
The range new user and group IDs are taken from, as
.Ar low Ns .. Ns Ar high .
Default 1000..60000.
.It Cm shell
The login shell.
Default
.Pa /bin/sh .
.It Cm skel_dir
The skeleton directory copied into new homes.
Default
.Pa /etc/skel .
.El
.Pp
.Ql useradd -D
prints the defaults, and with options rewrites this file.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/usermgmt.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/usermgmt.conf
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
base_dir	/home
shell		/bin/sh
group		=uid
range		1000..60000
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr useradd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file appeared in
.Nx 1.5 .
